SUMMARY:A Night in Venice - Toronto Operetta Theatre + Dinner (King Statio
 n)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\n**On Sunday\, April 19th\, join me for A N
 ight in Venice - Johann Strauss\, performed by the Toronto Operetta Theatr
 e\, and commissioned by** t**he Toronto Symphony Orchestra\, in associatio
 n with the Vancouver Symphony Orchestra\, TO Live\, and the National Arts 
 Centre’s National Creation Fund.** Set in “the most beautiful city in 
 the world\, this sparkling operetta by “Waltz King” Johann Strauss II 
 unfolds during Carnival\, where disguises\, romance\, and waltzes come to 
 life along the city’s iconic canals. The story follows the flirtatious D
 uke\, his scheming barber\, and a cascade of mistaken identities involving
  senators\, cooks\, and cabaret singers. Amid gondolas\, masked balls\, an
 d romantic entanglements\, chaos unfolds as characters swap roles to pursu
 e love or ambition. With Strauss’s sparkling waltzes and comedic twists\
 , the operetta celebrates charm\, deception\, and the joy of revelry. My s
 eat is Left Orchestra Seat P9. **Purchase A Night in Venice on Sunday\, Ap
 ril 19th at 3pm.**\n\n**COST**\nAdults: $51.75/ 86/ 107 + service charges\
 n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\n\nTicket Policy: All sales are final.\n\n**SI
 GNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP\, confirming if you will join for dinner after**\n*
  **[Purchase](https://www.ticketmaster.ca/toronto-operetta-theatre-night-i
 n-venice-toronto-ontario-04-19-2026/event/100062F70DA86374)**[ ](https://t
 ickets.mirvish.com/tina/20416)**your own ticket for Sunday April 19\, 2026
  at 3pm\, and post a comment with your seat number**\n\nA reminder will be
  sent the day before with my cell and reminder details where to meet and w
 hen.\n\nRSVPs close 1 day prior and cancellations will result in a No Show
  and impact future attendance.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me at: 2:45pm in
 side The Jane Mallett Theatre at 27 Front St. E.\, to the right side after
  scanning your tickets**\n\nStart: 3pm\n\nLength: 2.5 hours including an i
 ntermission\n\nAfter: meet at the same spot to head across the street to a
  local restaurant to chat about the show\n\nEnjoy and please post your com
 ments in the Event after.
